<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12118" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cydōnĭa</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cydōnēa</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κυδωνία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an ancient and
				celebrated town on the north coast of Crete</i>, now <i>Canea</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 7,
				12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12, 20, § 59</span></i> Sillig
				<i>N. cr.;</i>
			<i><span class="en">Flor. 3,
				7, 4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cydon</span></b> ,
				ōnis, m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A Cydonian</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
				12, 858</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A son of Phorcus</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
				10, 325</span></i>.—In plur., <i><span class="en">Luc. 7,
			229</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cydō-nĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., Cydonian</i>: spicula, <b>poet.</b> for <i>Cretan</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 10,
				59</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arcus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 9, 17</span></i>
			.—So esp. freq. Cydonia (and Latinized cotonia,
			cotonea) mala; also <i>absol.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cydōnĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏtōnĭa</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏtōnĕa</span></b> ),
				ōrum, n., <i>a
				quince</i> or <i>quince-apple</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 15,
				11, 10, § 37</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 5,
				10, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 7, 6</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 59</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 12,
				47, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 3</span></i> (4), 13, 27.—Cydonia
			arbor, or <i>absol.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cydōnĭus</span></b> ,
			ii, f., <i>a
			quince-tree</i>, <i><span class="en">Pall. Febr. 25, 21</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">25, 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Insit. 99
				al.</span></i>—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cydōnĕum</span></b> ,
			i, n., <i>quincejuice,
				quince-wine</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 33, 6,
			9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cy-dōnēus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., Cydonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juvencae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 1, 293</span></i>
			: pharetrae, <b>poet.</b> for <i>Cretan</i>, <i><span class="en">id. M. 8, 22</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sagittae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 7, 339</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">harundo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					10, 261</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cydōnītes</span></b> ,
			ae, <i>adj., Cydonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vites,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 2, 2</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cy-dōnītes</span></b> ,
				ae, m. (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶνος</span>), <i>quince-wine</i> (cf. B.
				<i>fin.</i>), <i><span class="en">Pall. Oct.
			20</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>E.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cydōnĭātae</span></b> ,
				ārum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Cydonia</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 37,
				60, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 58, 83, §
		228</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
